{"toolCallId":"call_873db5369d8b48a6b0e4822bba2bc567","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"The completeness calculator always exits 0, so a CI job or pre-commit hook cannot fail a build on incomplete spec docs without parsing its text or JSON output. A --min-percent <N> option turns the reported percentage into an exit status while leaving the report byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` prints an `Overall Completion` percentage and then always exits 0, so a caller that wants to fail a build on incomplete docs has to parse the text or JSON report itself. Every such caller re-implements the same comparison, and each one breaks when the report wording changes.\n\n### Purpose\nLet a caller state the threshold it already knows it needs, so one exit status answers \"are these docs complete enough\" without changing a byte of what the script prints.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\nThe script reports a percentage today but no option controls its exit status. Run against a complete packet it prints 100% and exits 0; passing `--min-percent` today is a usage error, because the option falls through to the positional-argument branch.\n\n```text\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization\nSpec Folder: specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization\nFiles Analyzed: 1\nOverall Completion: 100%\nTotal Placeholders: 0\nTotal Content Lines: 98\nStatus: ✅ Excellent - Nearly complete\nEXIT=0\n\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 80 specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization\nERROR: Unexpected argument: 80\nUse --help for usage information\nEXIT=1\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Parse `--min-percent <N>` in the script's argument loop, accepting an integer from 0 to 100.\n- Exit 3 when the percentage the run reports is below N, and exit 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Keep stdout byte-identical with and without the option, in both text and `--json` modes.\n- Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range N with an error on stderr and exit 1, printing no report.\n- Document the option in the script's `--help` text and its trailing exit-code comment.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing the placeholder patterns, the percentage math or the status thresholds - the feature only adds an exit status, and touching the math would move every caller's baseline.\n- Wiring the option into `validate.sh` or any CI workflow - this packet ships the script option only, and a consumer decides where to use it.\n- Adding a test harness - the script has no test suite today, so verification stays manual command invocations recorded in `tasks.md`.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Add `MIN_PERCENT` global, the `--min-percent` case branch with validation, the threshold comparison before the final exit, and the `--help` and exit-code documentation |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--min-percent <N>` exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N. | On a fixture whose report reads `Overall Completion: 80%`, `--min-percent 90` exits 3. |\n| REQ-002 | `--min-percent <N>` exits 0 when the reported percentage is at or above N, and when the option is absent. | On the same 80% fixture, `--min-percent 70` exits 0, and a run with no option exits 0. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-003 | The report is unchanged by the option, in text and JSON modes. | `diff` of stdout from a plain run and a `--min-percent` run is empty, for both default and `--json` output. |\n| REQ-004 | An invalid N is rejected before any report is printed. | `--min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc` and `--min-percent 101` each print an `ERROR:` line to stderr, exit 1, and print no report. |\n| REQ-005 | `--help` documents the option. | `--help` lists `--min-percent <N>` and states the 0-100 range and the exit-3 meaning. |\n| REQ-006 | The option works in `--file` mode against that file's `Completion` percentage. | `--file <path> --min-percent 90` on a file reporting 80% exits 3; `--min-percent 70` on it exits 0. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: On a fixture whose report reads `Overall Completion: 80%`, `--min-percent 90` exits 3 and `--min-percent 70` exits 0, with stdout identical in both runs.\n- **SC-002**: A run with no `--min-percent` exits 0 and produces stdout byte-identical to the pre-change script.\n- **SC-003**: `bash -n` on the script exits 0, and `--help` names the option.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required for the percentage math | Script exits 1 before calculating, so the new option cannot be exercised | Leave the existing `bc` guard in place; it already fails closed |\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 compatibility, which the script explicitly preserves | A `[[ ]]` or array construct that needs Bash 4 breaks macOS callers | Use a plain `case` branch and integer `[[ ]]` comparison only, then run `bash -n` |\n| Risk | A caller treats any non-zero exit as a crash and reports a false failure | High | Document exit 3 in `--help` and the trailing exit-code comment so the code is discoverable |\n| Risk | The threshold check accidentally changes stdout, breaking existing parsers | High | Diff a plain run against a `--min-percent` run in both text and JSON modes before closing |\n| Risk | An empty `MIN_PERCENT` is compared as 0 under `set -u`, silently failing every run | High | Guard the comparison on `[[ -n \"$MIN_PERCENT\" ]]` and verify a plain run still exits 0 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does the threshold apply in `--file` mode, where the report says `Completion` rather than `Overall Completion`? Decision: yes, REQ-006 compares against that file's `Completion` percentage, so one option behaves the same in both modes.\n- Should an invalid N exit 2 to separate usage errors from threshold failures? Decision: no, exit 1 matches the script's existing usage errors, and exit 3 stays unique to a below-threshold run.\n- Should N accept a decimal such as `85.5`? Decision: no, the report is already rounded to a whole number by `printf \"%.0f\"`, so an integer is the honest input.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"The completeness calculator always exits 0, so a CI job or pre-commit hook cannot fail a build on incomplete spec docs without parsing its text or JSON output. A --min-percent <N> option turns the reported percentage into an exit status while leaving the report byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` prints an `Overall Completion` percentage and then always exits 0, so a caller that wants to fail a build on incomplete docs has to parse the text or JSON report itself. Every such caller re-implements the same comparison, and each one breaks when the report wording changes.\n\n### Purpose\nLet a caller state the threshold it already knows it needs, so one exit status answers \"are these docs complete enough\" without changing a byte of what the script prints.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\nThe script reports a percentage today but no option controls its exit status. Run against a complete packet it prints 100% and exits 0; passing `--min-percent` today is a usage error, because the option falls through to the positional-argument branch.\n\n```text\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization\nSpec Folder: specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization\nFiles Analyzed: 1\nOverall Completion: 100%\nTotal Placeholders: 0\nTotal Content Lines: 98\nStatus: ✅ Excellent - Nearly complete\nEXIT=0\n\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 80 specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization\nERROR: Unexpected argument: 80\nUse --help for usage information\nEXIT=1\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Parse `--min-percent <N>` in the script's argument loop, accepting an integer from 0 to 100.\n- Exit 3 when the percentage the run reports is below N, and exit 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Keep stdout byte-identical with and without the option, in both text and `--json` modes.\n- Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range N with an error on stderr and exit 1, printing no report.\n- Document the option in the script's `--help` text and its trailing exit-code comment.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing the placeholder patterns, the percentage math or the status thresholds - the feature only adds an exit status, and touching the math would move every caller's baseline.\n- Wiring the option into `validate.sh` or any CI workflow - this packet ships the script option only, and a consumer decides where to use it.\n- Adding a test harness - the script has no test suite today, so verification stays manual command invocations recorded in `tasks.md`.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Add `MIN_PERCENT` global, the `--min-percent` case branch with validation, the threshold comparison before the final exit, and the `--help` and exit-code documentation |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--min-percent <N>` exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N. | On a fixture whose report reads `Overall Completion: 80%`, `--min-percent 90` exits 3. |\n| REQ-002 | `--min-percent <N>` exits 0 when the reported percentage is at or above N, and when the option is absent. | On the same 80% fixture, `--min-percent 70` exits 0, and a run with no option exits 0. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-003 | The report is unchanged by the option, in text and JSON modes. | `diff` of stdout from a plain run and a `--min-percent` run is empty, for both default and `--json` output. |\n| REQ-004 | An invalid N is rejected before any report is printed. | `--min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc` and `--min-percent 101` each print an `ERROR:` line to stderr, exit 1, and print no report. |\n| REQ-005 | `--help` documents the option. | `--help` lists `--min-percent <N>` and states the 0-100 range and the exit-3 meaning. |\n| REQ-006 | The option works in `--file` mode against that file's `Completion` percentage. | `--file <path> --min-percent 90` on a file reporting 80% exits 3; `--min-percent 70` on it exits 0. |\n| REQ-007 | When `--json` and `--min-percent` are passed together, the JSON output gains a boolean `min_percent_met` field, true when `Overall Completion` is at or above N and false otherwise. | `bash C --json --min-percent 70 \"$F\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true` and `bash C --json --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": false`; a `--json` run without the option prints no such field. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: On a fixture whose report reads `Overall Completion: 80%`, `--min-percent 90` exits 3 and `--min-percent 70` exits 0, with stdout identical in both runs.\n- **SC-002**: A run with no `--min-percent` exits 0 and produces stdout byte-identical to the pre-change script.\n- **SC-003**: `bash -n` on the script exits 0, and `--help` names the option.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required for the percentage math | Script exits 1 before calculating, so the new option cannot be exercised | Leave the existing `bc` guard in place; it already fails closed |\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 compatibility, which the script explicitly preserves | A `[[ ]]` or array construct that needs Bash 4 breaks macOS callers | Use a plain `case` branch and integer `[[ ]]` comparison only, then run `bash -n` |\n| Risk | A caller treats any non-zero exit as a crash and reports a false failure | High | Document exit 3 in `--help` and the trailing exit-code comment so the code is discoverable |\n| Risk | The threshold check accidentally changes stdout, breaking existing parsers | High | Diff a plain run against a `--min-percent` run in both text and JSON modes before closing |\n| Risk | An empty `MIN_PERCENT` is compared as 0 under `set -u`, silently failing every run | High | Guard the comparison on `[[ -n \"$MIN_PERCENT\" ]]` and verify a plain run still exits 0 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does the threshold apply in `--file` mode, where the report says `Completion` rather than `Overall Completion`? Decision: yes, REQ-006 compares against that file's `Completion` percentage, so one option behaves the same in both modes.\n- Should an invalid N exit 2 to separate usage errors from threshold failures? Decision: no, exit 1 matches the script's existing usage errors, and exit 3 stays unique to a below-threshold run.\n- Should N accept a decimal such as `85.5`? Decision: no, the report is already rounded to a whole number by `printf \"%.0f\"`, so an integer is the honest input.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_88ddf880b87d457c9c7aa8d8351899d8","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `C` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `F` is the 80% fixture folder described in `plan.md` section 5, built under `$TMPDIR`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Record the baseline report from the unmodified script (`C`). Verify: `bash C specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization > /tmp/baseline.txt` exits 0 and `grep 'Overall Completion' /tmp/baseline.txt` prints `Overall Completion: 100%`.\n- [ ] T002 Confirm the script parses cleanly before the change (`C`). Verify: `bash -n C` exits 0.\n- [ ] T003 Build the 80% fixture (`$TMPDIR/min-percent-fixture/spec.md`). Verify: `bash C \"$F\"` prints `Overall Completion: 80%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Declare the option global (`C`). Add `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` beside `VERBOSE`, `JSON_OUTPUT` and `QUALITY_CHECK` in section 3, so `set -u` never sees it unset.\n- [ ] T005 Add the argument branch (`C`). In the section 8 `case \"$1\"` block, add `--min-percent` that consumes `$2` and rejects a missing value with `ERROR: --min-percent requires a value` on stderr and exit 1; validate the value is an integer from 0 to 100 and reject anything else with `ERROR: --min-percent must be an integer between 0 and 100` and exit 1. Verify: `bash C --min-percent abc \"$F\"` prints the error and exits 1.\n- [ ] T006 Add the threshold comparison (`C`). After the `output_json` / `output_text` call and before the final `exit 0`, compare the reported percentage against `MIN_PERCENT` only when `MIN_PERCENT` is non-empty, exiting 3 when the report is below it. Use `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the stats-file `percentage` in `--file` mode. Verify: `bash C --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` exits 3.\n- [ ] T007 Document the option in `show_help` (`C`). Add `--min-percent <N>` with the 0-100 range and the exit-3 meaning. Verify: `bash C --help | grep -- '--min-percent'` prints one line.\n- [ ] T008 Extend the trailing exit-code comment (`C`). Add `3 - Overall Completion below --min-percent` under the existing `0` and `1` entries. Verify: `tail -5 C | grep -c '3 -'` prints `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Syntax check (`C`). Verify: `bash -n C` exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Below-threshold run (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` exits 3 and still prints the full report including `Overall Completion: 80%`.\n- [ ] T011 At-or-above-threshold run (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 70 \"$F\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Plain run unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C \"$F\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 Text output unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `diff <(bash C \"$F\") <(bash C --min-percent 70 \"$F\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T014 JSON output unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `diff <(bash C --json \"$F\") <(bash C --json --min-percent 70 \"$F\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T015 Invalid values rejected (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 101 \"$F\"`, `bash C --min-percent abc \"$F\"` and `bash C --min-percent` each exit 1 and print no report.\n- [ ] T016 `--file` mode threshold (`C`, `F/spec.md`). Verify: `bash C --file \"$F/spec.md\" --min-percent 90` exits 3 and `--min-percent 70` exits 0.\n- [ ] T017 Update documentation (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `diff` of plain-run stdout against `--min-percent` stdout is empty in both text and `--json` modes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `C` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `F` is the 80% fixture folder described in `plan.md` section 5, built under `$TMPDIR`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Record the baseline report from the unmodified script (`C`). Verify: `bash C specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization > /tmp/baseline.txt` exits 0 and `grep 'Overall Completion' /tmp/baseline.txt` prints `Overall Completion: 100%`.\n- [ ] T002 Confirm the script parses cleanly before the change (`C`). Verify: `bash -n C` exits 0.\n- [ ] T003 Build the 80% fixture (`$TMPDIR/min-percent-fixture/spec.md`). Verify: `bash C \"$F\"` prints `Overall Completion: 80%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Declare the option global (`C`). Add `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` beside `VERBOSE`, `JSON_OUTPUT` and `QUALITY_CHECK` in section 3, so `set -u` never sees it unset.\n- [ ] T005 Add the argument branch (`C`). In the section 8 `case \"$1\"` block, add `--min-percent` that consumes `$2` and rejects a missing value with `ERROR: --min-percent requires a value` on stderr and exit 1; validate the value is an integer from 0 to 100 and reject anything else with `ERROR: --min-percent must be an integer between 0 and 100` and exit 1. Verify: `bash C --min-percent abc \"$F\"` prints the error and exits 1.\n- [ ] T006 Add the threshold comparison (`C`). After the `output_json` / `output_text` call and before the final `exit 0`, compare the reported percentage against `MIN_PERCENT` only when `MIN_PERCENT` is non-empty, exiting 3 when the report is below it. Use `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the stats-file `percentage` in `--file` mode. Verify: `bash C --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` exits 3.\n- [ ] T007 Document the option in `show_help` (`C`). Add `--min-percent <N>` with the 0-100 range and the exit-3 meaning. Verify: `bash C --help | grep -- '--min-percent'` prints one line.\n- [ ] T008 Extend the trailing exit-code comment (`C`). Add `3 - Overall Completion below --min-percent` under the existing `0` and `1` entries. Verify: `tail -5 C | grep -c '3 -'` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T009 Emit the threshold verdict in JSON output (`C`, REQ-007). In `output_json`, when `JSON_OUTPUT` is set and `MIN_PERCENT` is non-empty, add a boolean `min_percent_met` field that is true when the reported percentage is at or above `MIN_PERCENT` and false otherwise, leaving every other field untouched. Verify: `bash C --json --min-percent 70 \"$F\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true` and `bash C --json --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": false`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Syntax check (`C`). Verify: `bash -n C` exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Below-threshold run (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` exits 3 and still prints the full report including `Overall Completion: 80%`.\n- [ ] T011 At-or-above-threshold run (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 70 \"$F\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Plain run unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C \"$F\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 Text output unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `diff <(bash C \"$F\") <(bash C --min-percent 70 \"$F\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T014 JSON output unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `diff <(bash C --json \"$F\") <(bash C --json --min-percent 70 \"$F\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T015 Invalid values rejected (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 101 \"$F\"`, `bash C --min-percent abc \"$F\"` and `bash C --min-percent` each exit 1 and print no report.\n- [ ] T016 `--file` mode threshold (`C`, `F/spec.md`). Verify: `bash C --file \"$F/spec.md\" --min-percent 90` exits 3 and `--min-percent 70` exits 0.\n- [ ] T017 Update documentation (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `diff` of plain-run stdout against `--min-percent` stdout is empty in both text and `--json` modes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
